gust 21, 1983.","t_chg":"Augusta's nights cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 151 complete years: Augusta's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.28\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.34 to \u22120.22), about \u22124.2\u00b0F since 1875. Augusta's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.22\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.26), about +3.2\u00b0F since 1875. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.49\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.11 to +0.88) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.47\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.09 to +0.85). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 12 months fell. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Augusta's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.13 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 44.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1929 (73.82 in); the driest, 1933 (28.05 in). Augusta almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.8 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}